    "id": "VSME:0102",
    "problem": "How does ten23 health provide fair compensation, employee representation, and development despite having no formal collective bargaining agreement and incomplete training-hour data?",
    "solution": "All employees are paid above the applicable living and cantonal minimum wages, permanent staff share a bonus programme, and employee ownership is available. Two employee representatives support dialogue without a formal collective agreement. Training time is not comprehensively tracked, but each new employee receives at least 14 onboarding hours, 83% completed Profile Dynamics assessments, and 20% had individual growth plans by year-end.",
    "attempt": "To address the issue of how Ten23 Health can provide fair compensation, employee representation, and development opportunities despite lacking a formal collective bargaining agreement and incomplete training-hour data, we need to consider several strategic approaches:\n\n### 1. Fair Compensation\n- **Market Research**: Conduct thorough market research to understand industry standards for compensation in similar roles and locations. This can help ensure that the company's pay scales are competitive.\n- **Performance-Based Incentives**: Implement performance-based incentives and bonuses to reward employees based on their contributions and achievements. This can include profit-sharing plans or commission structures where applicable.\n- **Regular Reviews**: Establish regular review processes to assess and adjust salaries based on performance, cost of living adjustments, and other relevant factors.\n\n### 2. Employee Representation\n- **Employee Councils**: Form an employee council or similar body where employees can voice their concerns and suggestions. This can be a platform for informal discussions and feedback.\n- **Open Communication Channels**: Maintain open lines of communication through regular meetings, newsletters, and suggestion boxes. Encourage managers to hold one-on-one meetings with their team members.\n- **Surveys and Feedback Mechanisms**: Use surveys and other feedback mechanisms to gather input from employees about their experiences and needs within the organization.\n\n### 3. Development Opportunities\n- **Mentorship Programs**: Develop mentorship programs where experienced employees can guide newer staff members, fostering skill development and career growth.\n- **Online Learning Resources**: Provide access to online learning platforms and resources that employees can use at their own pace to enhance their skills.\n- **Job Rotation**: Implement job rotation programs that allow employees to gain experience in different areas of the business, broadening their skill sets and career prospects.\n\n### Addressing Incomplete Training-Hour Data\n- **Data Collection Systems**: Invest in robust data collection systems to track training hours accurately. This could involve integrating time-tracking software into existing HR systems.\n- **Training Logs**: Require employees to maintain detailed logs of their training activities, which can then be reviewed and verified periodically.\n- **Regular Audits**: Conduct regular audits to ensure compliance with training requirements and to identify any gaps in the data collection process.\n\nBy implementing these strategies, Ten23 Health can create a more equitable and supportive work environment even without a formal collective bargaining agreement or complete training-hour data. The key is to focus on transparency, continuous improvement, and proactive engagement with employees.",
    "question_type": "non_factoid",
    "category": "VS/VSME",
    "grading": "No"
  },
