    "problem": "How should a sole trader with no governance body treat C9, and must the non-disclosure be identified in B1 as though information had been protected under paragraph 22?",
    "solution": "C9 applies only if the undertaking has a governance body in place. Because the sole trader has none, the gender diversity ratio is not applicable and may be omitted; under the if applicable principle, that omission is assumed to mean the item is not applicable. This is not an omission made under paragraph 22 for commercial prejudice, trade secrets, classified information, legal protection, privacy or security. Therefore, B1 does not require the undertaking to identify the omitted C9 datapoint as a paragraph 22 omission.",
